\fs32\b Scans\b0\fs20\par
\par
The original index scan is displayed in the separate ScanView window. The scan is the source from which entries are transcribed and later verified.\par
\par
\fs24\b Displaying a scan\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 can automatically locate and display the scan associated with the transcription when sufficient information is available to identify it.\par
\par
In Options you can choose whether WinBMD2 should automatically display the scan. When automatic scan display is enabled, the appropriate scan will normally be shown without needing to request it manually.\par
\par
If you prefer to control when scans are displayed, turn this option off and use the Scan commands when you want to display the scan.\par
\par
\fs24\b The ScanView window\b0\fs20\par
ScanView is a separate window from the transcription grid. The two windows can be resized and positioned independently.\par
\par
This allows the grid and scan to be arranged to suit the available screen space, or placed on separate monitors when more than one monitor is available.\par
\par
WinBMD2 remembers the size and position of the ScanView window.\par
\par
\fs24\b Viewing the scan\b0\fs20\par
The scan can be zoomed so that the index entries are large enough to read comfortably.\par
\par
You can move around a magnified scan to bring the required part of the page into view. The scan can also be rotated when the original image is not correctly orientated.\par
\par
The available Scan commands provide controls for adjusting the view and returning it to a suitable size or position.\par
\par
\fs24\b Finding scans\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 uses the source information in the transcription to locate the corresponding FreeBMD scan. When a suitable scan has already been downloaded, WinBMD2 can use the local copy rather than downloading it again.\par
\par
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "winbmdhelp://findingscans"}}{\fldrslt{\ul More about finding scans...}}}\par
\par
\fs24\b During transcription\b0\fs20\par
Position and magnify the scan so that the entries being transcribed can be read clearly while entering them into the grid.\par
\par
The ScanView window can remain open throughout transcription and verification.\par
\par
\fs24\b During verification\b0\fs20\par
When Verify is selected, the verification boxes appear below the scan. These can be positioned and resized to line up with the columns in the scanned index.\par
\par
See the Verification topic for details of checking the completed transcription against the scan.\par
\par
\fs24\b The ruler\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 includes a ruler which can help identify and follow individual lines on a scan.\par
\par
See the Ruler topic for instructions on setting up and using the ruler.\par
